  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Three cards are drawn from a standard deck of 52 cards without replacement. Find the probability that at least one of the cards is:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p9-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "a red card",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{15}{17}$",
          "worked": "There are 26 non-red cards. Let $R$ be the event of obtaining at least one red card.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(R')&=\\frac{26}{52}\\times\\frac{25}{51}\\times\\frac{24}{50}\\\\\\Pr(R')&=\\frac{2}{17}\\\\\\Pr(R)&=1-\\frac{2}{17}\\\\\\Pr(R)&=\\frac{15}{17}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "a king",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1201}{5525}$",
          "worked": "There are 48 non-kings. Let $K$ be the event of obtaining at least one king.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(K')&=\\frac{48}{52}\\times\\frac{47}{51}\\times\\frac{46}{50}\\\\\\Pr(K')&=\\frac{4324}{5525}\\\\\\Pr(K)&=1-\\frac{4324}{5525}\\\\\\Pr(K)&=\\frac{1201}{5525}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "a red king.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{25}{221}$",
          "worked": "There are two red kings, so 50 cards are not red kings. Let $T$ be the event of obtaining at least one red king.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(T')&=\\frac{50}{52}\\times\\frac{49}{51}\\times\\frac{48}{50}\\\\\\Pr(T')&=\\frac{196}{221}\\\\\\Pr(T)&=1-\\frac{196}{221}\\\\\\Pr(T)&=\\frac{25}{221}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      }
    ]
  },
